<%# Two columns fewer, measured. At 1024px - Tailwind's `lg`, where every column hidden below it appears at
    once - the sidebar leaves this table a 718px scroller and it wanted 927px, so the row actions sat off
    screen. Neither column that went says anything a reader acts on here:

    **ID** was 62px and is in the URL of the link in the same row - design.md has moved an id off a page
    twice for that reason. **Website** was 185px, already reduced to a host to stop it being the widest cell
    in the app, and it is a field on the stock's own page, which is where the record shape keeps an attribute
    the form edits.

    **Archived stays**, and that is the correction to the recommendation this came from: `#index` lists
    `Stock.all`, so this table mixes archived and active rows and the column is the only thing telling them
    apart. Dropping it would have hidden real state - and the two columns above are enough on their own,
    680px against a 718px scroller.

    Fewer columns rather than a third breakpoint: this app has two tiers, and the columns were the problem. %>
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Stocks",
                       description: "Prices refresh each weekday after the market closes, and this list " \
                                    "holds archived stocks as well as active ones." } do %>
    <%= link_to "New stock", new_admin_stock_path, class: admin_primary_button_class %>
  <% end %>

  <%= admin_table(
        @stocks,
        columns: [
          { attribute: :ticker, label: "Ticker", sortable: true },
          { attribute: :company_name, label: "Company name", sortable: true },
          { attribute: :current_price, label: "Current price", sortable: false },
          { attribute: :archived, label: "Archived", sortable: true }
        ],
        empty_message: "No stocks found. Create your first stock to get started."
      ) %>
</div>
